From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <MiaAI-Lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 13:55:47 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] feat(glm cuda): segmented KDA and DSA kernels for
 multi-stream verify windows (each segment its solo bits)

One verify window can hold several streams' rows back to back. Each segment runs from its own state with the
arithmetic of the single-stream decode kernels, so its rows get the bits of its window run alone:

- kda.cu / kda.py: chain_wide_segments (each segment from its state slot and parity into the other parity, its conv
  taps from its conv slot) and replay_layers_segments (each segment's kept rows); segment_table builds the int32
  table (first row, rows, slot, parity, conv slot, keep); 0-row segments are skipped, so one table and one CUDA
  graph per window size serve fewer streams
- forward.conv_shift_segments: each segment's conv window shifted by its own kept rows
- latent.py: seg_latent_write and seg_attention (dense rows over keys 0 .. pos of their stream's extent, sparse rows
  over their selected tokens, one chunk pass and one merge, the solo kernels' tiles and _tile math)
- sparse.py: seg_index_update (index keys, gates and the pools a row completes, at its stream's base) and
  seg_select_tokens (each sparse row's visible pools scored and selected by a split radix select: the same pools
  as top_pools); SPARSE_FROM and TOKENS name the dense limit and a sparse row's token list
- segments.py: SegRows (per-row position, extent base and kind, per-segment tables) and the selection's scratch
- forward.dsa_segments: dsa_block's latent path for such a window
- kda.reserve keeps the wide chain's scratch at its largest before graph capture (an outgrown pair stays alive)

The single-stream paths are unchanged.

Tests (GPU): tests/cuda/test_glm_kda_segments.py (chain, replay and conv shift against solo runs, torch.equal, at
real per-rank shapes, and against the one-kernel chain a decode window runs); tests/cuda/test_glm_attn_segments.py
(segmented DSA windows against each segment alone through the decode path, eager and graph, dense, across the dense
limit and sparse to 200k tokens; one graph per window size for any mix; dsa_segments against dsa_block; selection
kernels against the stable-sort reference; absorb, expand and matmul rows independent of the window).

From the GLM-5.3-Flash EXL3 2x DGX Sparks recipe (MiaAI-Lab), patches 0026 and 0029.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

